\b Step 1 - \b0\i0\ulnone \i Explain who might use the prediction and who may be affected by the system.\b0\i0\ulnone \b0\i0\ulnone \par
\par
\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i This application is intended for use on adult inpatients. Ingest removes patients outside the age range specified in the config (18 to 100 years of age) and patients whose sex is not on the allowed list in the config (Female or Male). Thus, patients outside these criteria are not covered by this system at all. Direct users of this system are the people planning discharge from hospital of the patients covered by this system: ward doctors, ward nurses, hospital discharge planners and hospital care co-ordinators. In addition, hospital managers and quality assurance personnel will use the totals generated by this application to plan for the follow-up care of their patients. Patients, families and carers of patients will also be affected. As patients who have been flagged for follow-up are passed from hospital to community based primary care and tertiary care, the flagged patients become the workload of GPs and community based nurses.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
