\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i Before any real use, a named person would need to approve it. This solution must be tested on real hospital data, checked for fairness across sex and age bands, and signed off by individuals responsible for clinical safety and privacy. The model would flag patients who need extra monitoring, but a clinician would make the decision and could override the model\u8217?s recommendations. The owner of the model would be responsible for monitoring its performance and retraining or withdrawing it as necessary. Before real use, approval would also need to follow the CARE principles, so Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people would have authority over how their data is used and the model would need to show collective benefit for their communities.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
