\i Step 3 - Select and justify a suitable train-validation-test or other evaluation strategy.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
\par
\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i Five percent of the cleaned patients are set aside at ingest as new patients, and the rest are split 80/20 into training and test rows. There is no separate validation set. For training rows five-fold cross-validation is used to compare models and drive the approval gate, while test rows are scored once after that. The split is stratified. This means the resulting split has readmission rates of about 14% in both the training and test sets. The split also uses the seed in config.yaml at every stage. A random split was the only option, since there is no date or site column, so results may look better than they would on a later period or a different hospital.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
