\par
\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i The primary metric of interest for this problem is ROC AUC, since the goal is to rank patients from most likely to be readmitted to least likely to be readmitted. Recall and precision are reported, since both a failure to predict a readmission and a false alarm are costly. Accuracy is reported but can be misleading, as only 14% of patients are readmitted. The implication is that a model that predicts no readmission for everyone would be correct 86% of the time. On the test set the logistic regression achieves an AUC of 0.639, with a recall of 0.616 and a precision of 0.224. The do-nothing baseline achieves an AUC of 0.500.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
