\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i Runs are logged locally to a database file (mlflow.db). The report files are overwritten on each run, so MLflow keeps the history. The train, evaluate and compare stages log their settings, scores and output files. Each run is tagged with the Git commit ID and the fingerprints of the data, config and model it used. Outputs go to fixed folders: model.joblib and model_card.json in artifacts, and the reports in reports. The database isn\u8217?t committed to Git, because the history belongs to the machine that generated it.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
