\i Step 4 - Record relevant information such as: model and preprocessing versions; parameters; evaluation metrics; data or dataset version; configuration; saved model artefacts; experiment results.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
\par
\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i Each train, evaluate and compare run is recorded in MLflow with its parameters (model settings, feature rules, test size and random seed), its scores, and tags for the Git commit and the fingerprints of the raw data, cleaned data, config and model. The code and preprocessing version are recorded by the Git commit, as the feature step is saved in the model file as a reference to the code, so that commit has to be checked out to rebuild the same behaviour. Config.yaml is stored with every run, so the exact settings are saved with the results. The saved model and model card (model.joblib and model_card.json, which holds the model, data and config fingerprints) are saved in artifacts/ and copied to the training run, and the scores and comparison results are in reports/ and on the evaluate and compare runs. Library versions are printed in the train report but not stored in MLflow, and most are pinned only to a minimum.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
