\i Step 1 - Pipeline architecture diagram: describe model evaluation and benchmarking (the baseline and candidate comparison).\b0\i0\ulnone \par
\par
\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i The above script compares four different models on the same test data: a do-nothing model, an age 65 rule, a logistic regression, and a random forest model. To verify the differences between the models, each model ran with 5-fold cross-validation on the training set. The results on the test set were 0.639 for the logistic regression, 0.636 for the random forest, 0.511 for the age 65 rule, and 0.500 for the do-nothing model. After running the two top-scoring models on cross-validation (0.606 for logistic regression and 0.599 for random forest), there were no meaningful differences between them. The folds had a variability of about 0.02. A simpler model was chosen, logistic regression. The model scores are stored in model_comparison.csv, and the final recommendation is written to evaluation_evidence.md.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
\par
