\i Step 1 - Explain why the proposed architecture is suitable for a prediction task rather than presenting a generic machine learning pipeline.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
\par
\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i The purpose of this pipeline is to answer one simple question for adult inpatients: Will they be readmitted within 30 days of discharge? Readmission occurs in only 14% of cases, so classes are imbalanced. As such, the model is evaluated on AUC and recall scores on the test data, computed separately by age and sex groups. The data needed cleaning, as ingest removed 320 rows (i.e. sex = \u8220?Other\u8221? or age < 18 or age > 100). The validation step here runs 11 checks before training up the model. The model is tested on a separate test data split. Wrong answers here can be very bad for patients, so the model is required to improve on the baseline by at least 0.05 AUC in cross-validation and then have a named person sign off on the model. Both the predict.py script and the corresponding FastAPI service scripts reuse the training code of this pipeline to process new inpatients exactly as the training data was.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
