\i Step 3 - Interpret the results rather than reporting metric values alone.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
\par
\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i This is a weak model, to be used as a screening tool only. It found 159 of the 258 readmitted cases for a miss rate of 99/258 or 38%. However, it raised 552 false alarms so that only about 1 in 5 of the flags raised actually corresponded to a readmitted patient. The hit rate was 22% or 1.6 times that of a random model which had a hit rate of 14%. The AUC for this model was 0.639, the random forest model scored 0.636, so the extra complexity buys nothing. This model is to be used as a means to decide which cases to refer to a clinician for further assessment.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
