\i Step 3 - Discuss limitations of the evaluation, including what the results do and do not establish.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
\par
\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i These results show that the logistic regression finds some real signal on this data: it beats the baseline and the age rule, and the gap is bigger than the fold-to-fold noise. They do not show that it would work on real patients, because the data is synthetic. The test set is one split of 1,840 patients with 258 readmissions, so the AUC of 0.639 could easily be a few points either way (about 0.60 to 0.68 when the test rows were resampled). There was no date or site column, so testing over time or across hospitals was not possible, and fairness was only checked by sex and age band, so the results say nothing about other groups, children, or whether flagging patients would actually reduce readmissions.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
