\i Step 3 - Evaluate the models using at least one metric suited to the prediction task.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
\par
\b \i Answer:\b0\i0\ulnone  \i All the graphs in this evaluation use the same test data. The ROC curves have AUC values for the saved logistic regression of 0.639, the random forest of 0.636 and the age rule of 0.511 where 0.5 is chance. So all models perform only slightly better than chance. The precision-recall curves for rare events look rather poor and only show marginal improvement over the 14% readmission rate, which is the precision of a model that always flags all patients (and hence has 100% recall). The error grid for the saved logistic regression is shown in the figure below. It reports 159 readmissions found, 99 missed and 552 false alarms.\b0\i0\ulnone \par
